From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: keep the minimum positive Liuqin level visible

The desktop uses logical level 1 as the minimum visible brightness. The
M81 integer index calculation rounds it down to the table's off entry,
turning off the LEDs even though userspace requested a positive level.

Use the first nonzero table entry for this boundary. Keep logical zero
as backlight off, and preserve every other OEM level and the linear path.

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8866.c b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8866.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8866.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8866.c
@@ -138,6 +138,9 @@ static int ktz8866_map_brightness(struct ktz8866 *ktz, unsigned int level)
 		index = 1700 * level / 2047;
 	else
 		index = 1700 + 347 * (level - 2048) / 2047;
+	/* Do not round a positive request down to the table's off entry. */
+	if (level && !index)
+		index = 1;
 	return liuqin_bl_curve[index];
 }
 
